This file is the one path that `//go:embed dist/*` in internal/webui/assets.go
can always match.

The React build (`npm run build` in web/) writes into internal/webui/dist and
empties that directory first, so nothing in it is committed except this file,
and the Go toolchain rejects an embed pattern that matches no file at all.
Without this anchor a fresh checkout cannot `go build ./...` or
`go test ./...` until the frontend has been built once.

Vite copies web/public/ into the output verbatim after emptying it, so every
build puts this exact file back. The two copies, web/public/README and
internal/webui/dist/README, must stay byte-identical or a build would leave
the checkout dirty; internal/webui/assets_test.go and
scripts/check-static-assets.sh fail when they drift.

The server never serves it: internal/server/public.go only looks up asset
paths that contain a dot, so `/README` falls through to the SPA shell.
